# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets. First, and deliberately first.
#
# `ckb-fly/deploy/.key.<network>` is the deployment key: it owns the code cells,
# so anyone holding it can spend the capacity they locked. `.key.visitor` signs
# the page's transactions. Neither belongs in a repository — and a key that has
# ever been pushed should be treated as spent, because a force-push does not
# remove it from anyone who already fetched.
#
# `deploy/.key` (no suffix) is the dev chain's published key. It is not a secret
# — it is in CKB's own `resource/specs/dev.toml` — but it is ignored anyway, so
# that a real key never ends up there by accident.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
ckb-fly/deploy/.key
ckb-fly/deploy/.key.*
*.key
*.pem

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build output
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Rust. `ckb-fly/target` is ~1 GB of intermediate artifacts, and for the RISC-V
# target `cargo clean -p` does not even clear it — see the Makefile's comment.
target/
# The stripped RISC-V contract binaries the integration suite loads, plus the
# unstripped copies. Reproducible with `make build`; `make checksum` records the
# hashes a deployment depends on.
ckb-fly/build/
# The front-end bundle. `public/app.js` is generated from the `*.source.js` files
# beside it by `build.mjs` (esbuild), and embeds CCC, JoyID and their
# dependencies — so committing it would vendor a megabyte of minified
# third-party code. `make build-front-end` regenerates it.
ckb-fly/deploy/public/app.js

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Dependencies
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
.venv/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Chain state and the node that produced it
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A dev chain's data directory (~57 MB) and the CKB node built from source to
# create it. Both are local to this machine; the README explains how to make
# your own.
ckb-fly/.devnet/
.ckbnode/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Third-party trees
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `repo/` is upstream `MidTermDev/immortal-fruit-fly`, `ref/` is
# `nervosnetwork/ckb-script-templates`. Both are other people's code, both are
# reproducible from the archives beside them, and only fixture *regeneration*
# needs them: `scripts/gen_fixture.py` reads `../repo/sim/flysim.py`. The
# fixture itself is committed, so building and testing this repository does not
# need either tree.
repo/
ref/
*.tar.gz

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tooling state
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.workbuddy/
.workbuddy-ai/
.DS_Store
